#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Herd Behavior 🐑]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Tendency to follow and mimic actions of a larger group]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Often ignoring individual analysis 🤔❌]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Can lead to irrational decisions in finance 📉]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Herd behavior refers to the tendency of individuals to follow and mimic the actions of a larger group.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("This often occurs even when it goes against their own individual analysis or judgement.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("In the context of finance, herd behavior can lead to irrational investment decisions and contribute to market volatility.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Examples in Finance 💰]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Stock market bubbles 📈🫧]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Panic selling during market crashes 📉😨]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Fad investing in "hot" stocks or sectors 🔥]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("One example of herd behavior in finance is the formation of stock market bubbles. As more and more investors buy into a rising stock or sector, others follow suit, often disregarding fundamentals.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("On the flip side, during market crashes, herd behavior can manifest as panic selling, where investors rush to sell their holdings as they see others doing the same.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Herd behavior can also lead to fad investing, where investors flock to 'hot' stocks or sectors, driving prices up in the short term, but often leading to overvaluation and subsequent corrections.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Consequences 🙊]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Amplification of market movements 📈📉]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Mispricing of assets 💸≠📊]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Inefficient allocation of capital 🏭💸❌]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("The consequences of herd behavior in financial markets can be significant. It can amplify both positive and negative market movements, leading to greater volatility.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("Herd behavior can also contribute to the mispricing of assets, as prices become detached from their underlying fundamentals.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("Ultimately, this can lead to an inefficient allocation of capital, as resources flow into overvalued assets and away from undervalued ones.")
]
]

#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Mitigation Strategies 🛡️]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Conduct independent research 🔍]
#v(20pt)
#only("2-")[- Have a long-term investment plan 📅💹]
#v(20pt)
#only("3-")[- Be aware of psychological biases 🧠]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("To mitigate the effects of herd behavior in your own financial decisions, it's important to conduct independent research and analysis, rather than simply following the crowd.")
]
#only("2")[
